## A Sticky Situation: Dakota Honey Company's Recall Woes  
Out of the frying pan and into the jar, Dakota Honey Company takes the spotlight this week with a record number of recalls. Not one, not two, but five separate recalls, all within the same day (May 20, 2026). The culprit? Stainless steel dust and flakes, as well as shreds of plastic, in their spin honey products. One has to wonder how much metal flotsam needs to accumulate before it starts making its way into jars. Note to manufacturers: maybe consider a metal detector for the production line.   

## Foreign Objects and Undeclared Allergens: A Common Theme   
Joining Dakota Honey Company in the recall parade is FINESALER LLC, who managed to bottle glass with their Alain MILLIAT Orange Marmalade. And let's not forget Raja Foods and Vegetables Inc., whose Swad Masala Candy turned a rather unappetizing shade of undeclared Blue 1 and Yellow 6 food coloring. Undeclared allergens also made their rounds this week, with WE R NUTS LLC's chocolate bridge mix causing a stir thanks to hidden cashews, milk, and soy. Ferris Coffee and Nut Company didn't want to be left out, hiding wheat and soy in their Vanilla Bourbon Trail Mix.
